                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "At first glance, you'd think 'Flappy Boat'. But it's better than that. Basically you move the boat left and right with A/D or a controller (xbox 360), and then place and remove the moon in the sky with the mouse. When you place the moon it causes the water to lift up into a wave towards it. Combining your placement of the moon and the boat, you navigate around to  avoid rocks and missiles and collect coins. It's actually quite fun for a freebie, though it does start ramping up in difficulty significantly around level 6. \n\nI think this is worth checking out. I really like the music, and the physics seem to be fair.",
